{
  "description": "Resource files as the embed step writes them, each with the embedded bundle's manifest as a reader reads it: the project's configuration with the channel resolved to its id, the SDK options and their defaults, the build-time facts, and the files and updates hosts in a build against staging or the local stack alone. The embedded bundle's manifest is the bundle manifest, the same whether the embed step registered the bundle or not; embeddedBundleId is null when it did not. channelId is null in a build whose embed step ran without a token or offline and could not resolve the channel's name; that build registers nothing either. publicKeys are the project's public keys as the embed step re-encoded them for the platform the file is written for, so the platform's own API imports them with no ASN.1 handled on the device: each { der, keyId }, der the base64 of the PKCS #1 DER on iOS and of the SPKI DER on Android, keyId the fingerprint over the SPKI bytes, which a signature names.",
